<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- What a backup carries (Google's Auto Backup, Android 6 to 11; data_extraction_rules.xml says the same for 12 and
     later): the games' places (saves.xml) and the player's settings (settings.xml), and nothing else.

     The settings go because a blind or partially sighted player setting up a new phone needs their theme, text size,
     voice speed, time to answer and microphone setting back without sighted help, and because Share usage data turned
     off has to stay off: left out, a restored phone would start sharing again. Nothing in them says who the player
     is. Onboarding having been done comes with them, so the new phone doesn't welcome the player again (Android asks
     for the microphone afresh, from a game).

     Never in a backup: the usage data's random ID and the events waiting to be sent (no_backup/analytics/, so a
     restored phone starts with a new ID, as the privacy policy says), the packs (no_backup/packs/: they download
     again), and the cache. -->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="saves.xml" />
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="settings.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
